 174:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** 
 175:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** /**
 176:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** * @ingroup groupTransforms
 177:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** */
 178:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** 
 179:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** /**
 180:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * @defgroup RealFFT Real FFT Functions
 181:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  *
 182:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 183:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The CMSIS DSP library includes specialized algorithms for computing the
 184:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * FFT of real data sequences.  The FFT is defined over complex data but
 185:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * in many applications the input is real.  Real FFT algorithms take advantage
 186:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * of the symmetry properties of the FFT and have a speed advantage over complex
 187:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * algorithms of the same length.
 188:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 189:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The Fast RFFT algorith relays on the mixed radix CFFT that save processor usage.
 190:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 191:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The real length N forward FFT of a sequence is computed using the steps shown below.
 192:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 193:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \image html RFFT.gif "Real Fast Fourier Transform"
 194:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 195:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The real sequence is initially treated as if it were complex to perform a CFFT.
 196:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * Later, a processing stage reshapes the data to obtain half of the frequency spectrum
 197:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * in complex format. Except the first complex number that contains the two real numbers
 198:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * X[0] and X[N/2] all the data is complex. In other words, the first complex sample
 199:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * contains two real values packed.
 200:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 201:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The input for the inverse RFFT should keep the same format as the output of the
 202:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * forward RFFT. A first processing stage pre-process the data to later perform an
 203:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * inverse CFFT.
 204:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 205:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \image html RIFFT.gif "Real Inverse Fast Fourier Transform"
 206:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 207:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The algorithms for floating-point, Q15, and Q31 data are slightly different
 208:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * and we describe each algorithm in turn.
 209:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par Floating-point
 210:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The main functions are arm_rfft_fast_f32() and arm_rfft_fast_init_f32().
 211:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The older functions arm_rfft_f32() and arm_rfft_init_f32() have been
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccvMm3gs.s 			page 15


 212:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * deprecated but are still documented.
 213:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 214:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The FFT of a real N-point sequence has even symmetry in the frequency
 215:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * domain. The second half of the data equals the conjugate of the first
 216:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * half flipped in frequency. Looking at the data, we see that we can
 217:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * uniquely represent the FFT using only N/2 complex numbers. These are
 218:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * packed into the output array in alternating real and imaginary
 219:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * components:
 220:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 221:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * X = { real[0], imag[0], real[1], imag[1], real[2], imag[2] ...
 222:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * real[(N/2)-1], imag[(N/2)-1 }
 223:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 224:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * It happens that the first complex number (real[0], imag[0]) is actually
 225:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * all real. real[0] represents the DC offset, and imag[0] should be 0.
 226:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * (real[1], imag[1]) is the fundamental frequency, (real[2], imag[2]) is
 227:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * the first harmonic and so on.
 228:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 229:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The real FFT functions pack the frequency domain data in this fashion.
 230:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The forward transform outputs the data in this form and the inverse
 231:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * transform expects input data in this form. The function always performs
 232:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * the needed bitreversal so that the input and output data is always in
 233:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * normal order. The functions support lengths of [32, 64, 128, ..., 4096]
 234:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * samples.
 235:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par Q15 and Q31
 236:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The real algorithms are defined in a similar manner and utilize N/2 complex
 237:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * transforms behind the scenes.
 238:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 239:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The complex transforms used internally include scaling to prevent fixed-point
 240:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * overflows.  The overall scaling equals 1/(fftLen/2).
 241:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 242:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each transform used but
 243:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * twiddle factor and bit reversal tables can be reused.
 244:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 245:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
 246:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
 247:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
 248:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * - Initializes twiddle factor table and bit reversal table pointers.
 249:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * - Initializes the internal complex FFT data structure.
 250:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * \par
 251:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
 252:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure
 253:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * cannot be placed into a const data section. To place an instance structure
 254:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * into a const data section, the instance structure should be manually
 255:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * initialized as follows:
 256:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 257:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  *arm_rfft_instance_q31 S = {fftLenReal, fftLenBy2, ifftFlagR, bitReverseFlagR, twidCoefRModifier, 
 258:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  *arm_rfft_instance_q15 S = {fftLenReal, fftLenBy2, ifftFlagR, bitReverseFlagR, twidCoefRModifier, 
 259:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 260:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * where <code>fftLenReal</code> is the length of the real transform;
 261:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>fftLenBy2</code> length of  the internal complex transform.
 262:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>ifftFlagR</code> Selects forward (=0) or inverse (=1) transform.
 263:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>bitReverseFlagR</code> Selects bit reversed output (=0) or normal order
 264:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * output (=1).
 265:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>twidCoefRModifier</code> stride modifier for the twiddle factor table.
 266:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * The value is based on the FFT length;
 267:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>pTwiddleAReal</code>points to the A array of twiddle coefficients;
 268:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>pTwiddleBReal</code>points to the B array of twiddle coefficients;
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccvMm3gs.s 			page 16


 269:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * <code>pCfft</code> points to the CFFT Instance structure. The CFFT structure
 270:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * must also be initialized.  Refer to arm_cfft_radix4_f32() for details regarding
 271:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  * static initialization of the complex FFT instance structure.
 272:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c ****  */
 273:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_rfft_fast_f32.c **** 
